        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "ZEC.14.8"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Zech 14.8",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "REV.22.1+REV.22.2"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Rev 22.1-2",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Then he brought me back to the door of the temple; and behold, water was issuing from below the threshold of the temple toward the east (for the temple faced east); and the water was flowing down from below the south end of the threshold of the temple, south of the altar. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then he brought me out by way of the north gate, and led me round on the outside to the outer gate, that faces toward the east;",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47.2",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Heb obscure",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " and the water was coming out on the south side.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.2"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Going on eastward with a line in his hand, the man measured a thousand cubits, and then led me through the water; and it was ankle-deep. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Again he measured a thousand, and led me through the water; and it was knee-deep. Again he measured a thousand, and led me through the water; and it was up to the loins. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Again he measured a thousand, and it was a river that I could not pass through, for the water had risen; it was deep enough to swim in, a river that could not be passed through. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said to me, “Son of man, have you seen this?”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then he led me back along the bank of the river. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As I went back, I saw upon the bank of the river very many trees on the one side and on the other. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said to me, “This water flows toward the eastern region and goes down into the Arabah; and when it enters the stagnant waters of the sea,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47.8",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Compare Syr: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "into the sea to the sea those that were made to issue forth",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " the water will become fresh. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And wherever the river",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47.9",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Gk Syr Vg Tg: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "two rivers",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " goes every living creature which swarms will live, and there will be very many fish; for this water goes there, that the waters of the sea",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47.9",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Compare Syr: Heb lacks",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the waters of the sea",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " may become fresh; so everything will live where the river goes. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fishermen will stand beside the sea; from En-gedi to En-eglaim it will be a place for the spreading of nets; its fish will be of very many kinds, like the fish of the Great Sea. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But its swamps and marshes will not become fresh; they are to be left for salt. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And on the banks, on both sides of the river, there will grow all kinds of trees for food. Their leaves will not wither nor their fruit fail, but they will bear fresh fruit every month, because the water for them flows from the sanctuary. Their fruit will be for food, and their leaves for healing.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Thus says the Lord ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ": “These are the boundaries by which you shall divide the land for inheritance among the twelve tribes of Israel. Joseph shall have two portions. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And you shall divide it equally; I swore to give it to your fathers, and this land shall fall to you as your inheritance.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“This shall be the boundary of the land: On the north side, from the Great Sea by way of Hethlon to the entrance of Hamath, and on to Zedad,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47.15",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Gk: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the entrance of Zedad, Hamath",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Berothah, Sibraim (which lies on the border between Damascus and Hamath), as far as Hazer-hatticon, which is on the border of Hauran. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So the boundary shall run from the sea to Hazar-enon, which is on the northern border of Damascus, with the border of Hamath to the north.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47.17",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Heb obscure",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " This shall be the north side.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“On the east side, the boundary shall run from Hazar-enon",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47.18",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Cn: Heb lacks",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Hazar-enon",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " between Hauran and Damascus;",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47.18",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Heb obscure",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " along the Jordan between Gilead and the land of Israel; to the eastern sea and as far as Tamar.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47.18",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Compare Syr: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "you shall measure",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " This shall be the east side.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.18"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 47:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“On the south side, it shall run from Tamar as far as the waters of Meribath-kadesh, thence along the Brook of Egypt to the Great Sea. This shall be the south side.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.47.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.47.19"
            ]
          }
        }
